.TH "Hypoland" "1" "" "" "Hypoland User Manual"
.SH NAME
hypoland \- Dynamic tiling Wayland compositor for OpenGL ES 2.0 graphics
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]hypoland\f[R] [\f[I]arg [...]\f[R]].
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]Hypoland\f[R] is a fork of the Wayland compositor Hyprland for
graphics hardware that is limited to OpenGL ES 2.0, such as Intel GMA
X3100 and GMA 4500MHD.
.PP
It is an independent project and not affiliated with or endorsed by
Hyprland.
.PP
You can launch Hypoland by either going into a TTY and executing
\f[B]start\-hypoland\f[R], or with a login manager.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Hypoland reads the configuration of Hyprland and answers on the same
sockets, so configs and tools made for Hyprland keep working.
.PP
Color management, HDR, motion blur, the logo background, the default
wallpapers, plugins and hyprpm are removed.
Their config options are accepted and ignored.
Blur, shadows, animations and the splash text are off by default.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration is read from
\f[I]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypr/hyprland.lua\f[R].
.PP
For configuration information please see <*https://wiki.hypr.land*>.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\-\-help\f[R]
Show command usage.
.TP
\f[B]\-c\f[R], \f[B]\-\-config\f[R] \f[I]FILE\f[R]
Specify config file to use.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-socket\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Sets the Wayland socket name (for Wayland socket handover)
.TP
\f[B]\-\-wayland\-fd\f[R] \f[I]FD\f[R]
Sets the Wayland socket file descriptor (for Wayland socket handover)
.TP
\f[B]\-\-watchdog\-fd\f[R] \f[I]FD\f[R]
Used by start\-hypoland.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-safe\-mode\f[R]
Starts Hypoland in safe mode.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-systeminfo\f[R]
Prints system infos.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-i\-am\-really\-stupid\f[R]
Omits the check for root user privileges.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-verify\-config\f[R]
Do not run Hypoland, only print if the config has any errors.
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\-\-version\f[R]
Print the version.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-version\-json\f[R]
Print the version as JSON.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-locked\-cmd\f[R] \f[I]COMMAND\f[R]
Launches a locker on startup via the provided command.
